; worldtravel.eval — travel as a JOURNEY (P3, docs/world-map.md).
;
; What this measures, and why each line is where it is:
;   - a journey COSTS TIME by the square entered, and the costs are settled for
;     that span rather than accrued per frame. `step` is never used: nothing on
;     the world map ticks, so simulated seconds would prove nothing either way.
;   - supplies fall BECAUSE of the journey. `supplies` reports hours left, so
;     the before/after pair is the measurement.
;   - an impassable square REFUSES rather than clamping, and the travel command
;     reports what it did instead of what it was asked.
logecho on
reset

worldmap on
supplies
world

; --- east along the road, then into the hills: two different travel costs ----
travel e 3
travel n 2
world
supplies

; --- west into the water: the run must stop short and say so ----------------
worldpos 3 8
travel w 4
world

; --- discovery: walking within sight of a location finds it -----------------
; `worldpos` is a raw teleport (it applies no travel rules and discovers
; nothing), so the discovery below is the STEP's doing, not the placement's.
worldpos 10 8
world
travel s 1
world
